// https://www.x.org/releases/X11R7.7/doc/xproto/x11protocol.pdf
//
// `x11::connection` speaks the core X11 protocol without Xlib or xcb. Every
// socket operation goes through the thread's shared `io_uring` from
// `nix::alloc_io_uring_runtime()`, so a round trip is a linked send and
// receive submitted by a single `io_uring_enter`. Requests are buffered until a
// flush, a reply wait, or an event wait sends them.
//
// A `connection` and everything it returns belong to one thread.

namespace x11 {

